[h1]R.A.T.S. Keel 0.5 – drop the anchor, raise the keel[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. - Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

Keel keeps your modded game afloat. 0.5 is the biggest Keel update so far.

[h2][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459]What's new since your last game – right on the main menu[/url][/h2]
[list]
[*]A card splits off the Keel card and shows which mods are [b]new, updated, gone or broken[/b] since you last played
[*][b]The author's own words[/b]: Workshop change notes or the mod's changelog, one line each
[*]Click a mod for its full notes; right click and both cards get out of your way
[*]No more guessing what changed after a Workshop update night
[/list]

[h2]One loader, every mod once[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Keel takes over[/b] from Anchor Chain and Alpine's Mod Loader: no mod starts twice anymore
[*][b]Nothing to uninstall[/b]: their files stay as they are; switch Keel off and they start again
[*]Your Anchor Chain mods and BepInEx plugins keep running as they are
[/list]

[h2]Know which mod broke – and why[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Every mod checked against your game version[/b] before it starts
[*]A broken mod is marked, the rest of your list sails on
[*][b]The report[/b] (Ctrl+Shift+K): every mod, running or not, in plain words
[*][b]Send report[/b] in one click when you want me to look
[/list]

[h2]The game's mod warning, readable[/h2]
[list]
[*]The "not declared compatible" question now shows [b]short names[/b], code mods apart from data mods, and the version each one was made for
[*]No more wall of folder paths
[/list]

[h2]Euromod players[/h2]
[list]
[*]The report names your stage: Main Pack, + AC Pack, + Extended Guidance
[*][b]Extended Guidance on or off with one button[/b]
[/list]

[h2]Smaller stuff[/h2]
[list]
[*]Loading window sits top right and counts your mods while the game starts
[*]Right click hides the cards; they stay until then
[*]ALTERNATIVE MODS menu entry back on every start
[*]Works with Alternative Game Interface (menu clicks after the report)
[*]Mod makers: opt in to start early, before the load screen ends
[/list]

